{
 "_doc": "The aqua skin: the session-only early-2000s gel-and-pinstripe look the `someFruitCompany` cheat word (logoStage.json) toggles on the browser, the desktop and the extension. `tokens` are the CSS custom properties css/aqua/tokens.css declares (the stylesheet is the source of truth; tests/config/aqua.test.js pins this copy against it) and the desktop's aquaPalette reads them over the qrc alias. `aliases` are the base theme tokens the skin points at one of those (the same sheet, the same pin), which the desktop fills its sheet with in their place. `tint` is how the accent paints the gel: each token is the chosen accent mixed in sRGB toward its colour by its share (0 = the accent itself), `--aq-on-select` is the accent's on-colour over `--aq-select` and `--aq-on-gel` the one over the gel's deep half (`--aq-gel-bottom`), both by accents.js onAccentInk; the `tokens` above are that recipe over `base`, the Blue preset, the face before any accent is painted. `image` is the wallpaper the word paints when no image is loaded, on an integer `cell`-px grid so the two painters agree pixel for pixel: `ramp` is the base blue in equal bands top to bottom, and every swoosh a parabola of `span` cells from column `x0`, its crest `amp` cells above row `base`, `width` cells deep, painted later over earlier, its first and last `edge` rows a checker of `edgeColor` over what lies beneath. `word` is the STENCIL glyphs of webcore.json `word` in this skin's colours, laid `widthShare` wide and centred on `centerYShare` of the height.",
